  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Monday) \nIssued at 1049 AM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nMedium range guidance is suggesting the ridge will start to break \ndown towards the end of the week. This is being shown in the \ntemperature guidance starting Friday. Yes, it'll still be hot and \nhumid, but the heat risk should be slightly less. As we move into \nthe weekend and Labor Day, we continue to see temperatures back off \na bit as the ridge slips off to the west. Slightly above normal \nafternoon highs will probably still be with us, but not as intense \nas the middle of this week. The stinker is, if we start to lose the \nridge this weekend, that means low to medium storm chances will \nlikely start to creep back into the forecast. Nothing organized, but \ndiurnal, summer-time thunderstorms with at least a low wind risk \nwould re-enter the forecast.",
